'''Soul Eater''' is a [[buff]] that causes affected [[character]]s and [[monster]]s to '''Eat a Soul''' when they kill an enemy, gaining an '''Eaten Soul'''. Each eaten soul grants increased [[attack speed]], [[cast speed]], and [[character size]]. Enemy monsters and [[minion]]s also gain less damage taken per soul.

==Mechanics==
===Soul Eater===
The Soul Eater buff will cause the target to eat a soul of a nearby enemy when it dies. This buff will persist until the source of it expires. The effect does not stack or refresh, and Soul Eater cannot be gained while an entity already has Soul Eater. 

Soul Eater has a [[radius]] of 6 metres.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ovzG1UorA4Y|title=Soulthirst Juggernaut Build Guide
|author=wwwaldo333|date=Aug 19, 2018|accessdate=December 9, 2020|publisher=Youtube}}</ref> Killing enemies farther away than this will not give stacks.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/2475063|title=<nowiki>[3.6] The Broken Build | 40s Soul Eater & 80s Headhunter Buffs | Guaranteed to Crash Your Game |30ex </nowiki>|author=sodapop9|accessdate=14 January 2021|date=Narch 27, 2019}}</ref> Monsters which have Soul Eater still gain souls while invulnerable; however, monsters that burrow (e.g. Devourers) are often out of the range to gain souls.<ref>https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/3284453</ref>

===Eaten Souls===
Certain stats, items, or passives may grant the ability to {{c|mod|Eat # Soul(s)...}}; this grants the listed number of eaten souls and the equivalent bonuses, but does not grant the Soul Eater buff itself. The stacks are shared, however.

Each eaten soul grants 5% increased [[attack speed]], 5% increased [[cast speed]], and 1% increased [[character size]]. Note that the attack and cast speed bonuses are separate, which causes the {{c|mod|Increases and Reductions to Cast Speed apply to Attack Speed}} modifier from {{il|Wilma's Requital}} to gain double the attack speed from eaten souls. On monsters and [[minion]]s, each eaten soul also grants 2% less damage taken. 

Maximum number of eaten souls is capped at 45. The less damage taken effect from eaten souls is capped at 90%.

For players, an eaten soul is lost every 0.5 seconds if a soul has not been gained in the last 4 seconds. On non-player entities, a soul is lost every 0.2 seconds if a soul has not been gained in the last 2 seconds.

The number of eaten souls resets to 0 if a monster becomes possessed by a [[Tormented Spirit]].<ref>https://youtu.be/QNOCgoMZKBw?t=3025</ref>

==Sources==
Character or minions can use various items to gain a Soul Eater buff, or steal it from non-unique monsters using {{il|Headhunter}} or similar items.

